STATEMENT #3: InsertProductAsync - Transaction Block with SCOPE_IDENTITY
================================================================================
DMS Status: ERROR (not attempted due to consistent DMS failures)

Original SQL Server Statement:
DECLARE @NewProductId INT;

BEGIN TRANSACTION;
    INSERT INTO Products (Name, Description, Price, StockQuantity)
    VALUES (@Name, @Description, @Price, @StockQuantity);
    
    SET @NewProductId = SCOPE_IDENTITY();
    
    INSERT INTO ProductHistory (ProductId, Action, OldPrice, NewPrice, OldStock, NewStock, ActionDate)
    VALUES (@NewProductId, 'INSERT', NULL, @Price, NULL, @StockQuantity, GETDATE());
    
    UPDATE ProductStats
    SET 
        TotalProducts = TotalProducts + 1,
        AveragePrice = (AveragePrice * TotalProducts + @Price) / (TotalProducts + 1),
        LastUpdated = GETDATE()
    WHERE StatId = 1;
COMMIT;

SELECT @NewProductId;

Manual Conversion Applied: YES
Conversion Notes:
- CRITICAL: SCOPE_IDENTITY() replaced with RETURNING clause
- GETDATE() replaced with CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
- BEGIN TRANSACTION → BEGIN (PostgreSQL syntax)
- COMMIT remains same
- Variable declarations handled differently in PostgreSQL (using WITH)
- Transaction blocks in PostgreSQL don't support returning values directly

Manual PostgreSQL Conversion:
WITH inserted_product AS (
    INSERT INTO Products (Name, Description, Price, StockQuantity)
    VALUES (@Name, @Description, @Price, @StockQuantity)
    RETURNING ProductId
),
history_insert AS (
    INSERT INTO ProductHistory (ProductId, Action, OldPrice, NewPrice, OldStock, NewStock, ActionDate)
    SELECT ProductId, 'INSERT', NULL, @Price, NULL, @StockQuantity, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
    FROM inserted_product
    RETURNING ProductId
)
UPDATE ProductStats
SET 
    TotalProducts = TotalProducts + 1,
    AveragePrice = (AveragePrice * TotalProducts + @Price) / (TotalProducts + 1),
    LastUpdated = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
WHERE StatId = 1
RETURNING (SELECT ProductId FROM inserted_product);

Changes Made:
1. Replaced SCOPE_IDENTITY() with RETURNING clause in INSERT
2. Replaced GETDATE() with CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (3 occurrences)
3. Converted transaction block to use CTEs with RETURNING
4. Removed DECLARE and SET (using CTEs instead)
5. Changed BEGIN TRANSACTION/COMMIT structure

NOTE: This conversion requires C# code modification to handle the RETURNING clause properly.

