Manual PostgreSQL Conversion:
WITH old_values AS (
    SELECT Price as OldPrice, StockQuantity as OldStock
    FROM Products
    WHERE ProductId = @ProductId
),
product_update AS (
    UPDATE Products
    SET 
        Name = @Name,
        Description = @Description,
        Price = @Price,
        StockQuantity = @StockQuantity,
        ModifiedDate = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
    WHERE ProductId = @ProductId
    RETURNING ProductId
),
history_insert AS (
    INSERT INTO ProductHistory (ProductId, Action, OldPrice, NewPrice, OldStock, NewStock, ActionDate)
    SELECT @ProductId, 'UPDATE', ov.OldPrice, @Price, ov.OldStock, @StockQuantity, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
    FROM old_values ov
    RETURNING ProductId
)
UPDATE ProductStats
SET 
    AveragePrice = (AveragePrice * TotalProducts - (SELECT OldPrice FROM old_values) + @Price) / TotalProducts,
    LastUpdated = CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
WHERE StatId = 1;

Changes Made:
1. Replaced GETDATE() with CURRENT_TIMESTAMP (3 occurrences)
2. Converted DECLARE/SELECT pattern to CTE (old_values)
3. Removed BEGIN TRANSACTION/COMMIT (handled at application level)
4. Used CTEs to chain operations

